In the misty streets of Stranglethorn Vale, Elara, a young Gnome Warlock, found himself in a dilemma. While his pet Succubus, Nym, was a formidable companion capable of handling high-level quests, she was often too powerful for the average player. Elara, however, was a novice, and he needed a pet that could handle the basics without overwhelming him.

One rainy evening, Elara approached Nym, who was currently guarding a rare item. "Nym, I need you to take this to the vendor," Elara said, holding out a small, glowing orb. "It's a simple quest item, but it's very important to me."

Nym, usually arrogant and demanding, hesitated. She looked at the orb, then at Elara's trembling hands. "You are a novice, Elara," she growled, her voice dripping with disdain. "I am a pet. I do not need to be taught how to fetch a simple item."

Elara smiled gently. "Nym, you are not just a pet; you are my best friend. And you are the only one who can handle this quest."

Nym paused, her eyes narrowing. She remembered a forgotten, ancient skill she had learned from a dying elder in the past. It was a rare ability that made her more common than she ever thought possible. She lowered her guard, her tail wagging nervously. "Fine," she muttered, "but if I fail, you will be the first to die."

Elara nodded, ready to begin the quest.

